        "abstract": "In this project, we visualize and analyze data of Hybrid Accelerated Cosmology Code (HACC) cosmology simulations. We investigate in point rendering as well as Smoothed-particle hydrodynamics (SPH) interpolation and apply them to visualize the data in a 3D environment. Paraview was used for the rendering task. Some parameters of points in the software were adjusted to find well-qualified visualizations. These approaches provide a clear vision to the impact of Active Galactic Nuclei (AGN) on surrounding matter, and thus, we can gain more information for understanding the nature of AGNs and the universe.",
